export const meta = {
  name: 'multi-phase-drafts',
  description: 'Parallel design+draft for Phases 2/3/4/5 — each agent writes a spec + draft diff to /workspace/, NO main-tree writes (I vet+apply myself)',
  phases: [{ title: 'Draft', detail: '9 agents draft datasets, compile additions, verification harness, dead-code removal in parallel' }],
}
const SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', additionalProperties: false,
  required: ['phase','area','design_summary','draft_path','files_to_change','risks'],
  properties: {
    phase: { type: 'string' }, area: { type: 'string' },
    design_summary: { type: 'string', description: '6-12 sentences: the approach, grounded in actual file:line of the current code.' },
    draft_path: { type: 'string', description: 'Path under /workspace/ where you wrote the full design + draft code/diff.' },
    files_to_change: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'Exact main-tree files + line regions the real change will touch.' },
    risks: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
}
const COMMON = `Repo root: /workspace/SuperGrok1.5. You DESIGN + DRAFT only — write your full design and draft code/diff to a file under /workspace/ (NOT into the repo; the lead applies vetted drafts to the main tree himself — a hard rule). READ the actual current code first (cite file:line); the codebase is the source of truth. CPU-only (no GPU). PROJECT TRUTH: L3-TC persistent wgmma megakernel only; HARD gate = fp64(1e-4;SAM 2.5e-2)+A/A/A determinism; keep/revert ratchet; legal rewrites are transport-only (preserve ascending-k fp32 order); gfx942/tpu_v6e preserved. Model sizes: race decoder d128/h4/L2/vocab99/seq4, ViT patch49/16patch/d128/cls/classes97, Mamba d128/L2/state128/seq8; flagship decoder d1600/L48, ViT d1664/L48, mamba d2048/L24. The current data is mod-97 (grokking_race_v2.py: make_data_for_task@372, evaluate@536 forwards WHOLE tensor, EarlyStopper@542 stops on VAL acc>=0.95). Make your draft CONCRETE and minimal-diff against the real code.`

const agents = [
  // ---- Phase 3: datasets ----
  { name:'p3_decoder_fineweb', phase:'P3', label:'P3 decoder/FineWeb-Edu', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT: wire FineWeb-Edu into the DECODER cell. Single-pass STREAMING (HF datasets streaming=True OR the sample-10BT subset ~27GB on /workspace), BPE (~50K vocab) pre-tokenized to uint16 with a few-GB rolling buffer; causal-LM next-token CE at every position. A FIXED SMALL held-out eval probe (~1-10M tokens) sampled ONCE at load and reused identically every eval (NEVER iterate the full split). Respect the existing model dims (decoder vocab is currently 99 — note the vocab change to ~50K means the embedding/head resize; flag how the model def handles vocab — do NOT change model defs, but document the coupling). Output: the make_data_for_task decoder branch returning (train_stream iterator, fixed_eval_probe) + how it plugs into fused_train_step (tokens/targets int32). Write design+draft to /workspace/phase3/decoder_fineweb.md.` },
  { name:'p3_vit_imagenet', phase:'P3', label:'P3 vit/ImageNet-1k', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT: wire ImageNet-1k into the ViT cell. Download full (~150GB) to /workspace (random-access aug wants it local; budget re-sees <1 epoch so safe) OR timm/imagenet-1k-wds. 1000-way classification from CLS, CE + standard aug. FIXED held-out probe = the standard 50k val subset sampled once, reused every eval (cap eval to seconds). Note the current ViT patch=49/num_patches=16/classes=97 — ImageNet is 224x224/patch16/1000 classes, a model-size coupling (document it; do NOT change model defs, flag the resize). Keep the accuracy early-stop trigger for this cell (top-1). Output: make_data_for_task vit branch + fixed val probe. Write to /workspace/phase3/vit_imagenet.md.` },
  { name:'p3_mamba_gifteval', phase:'P3', label:'P3 mamba/GiftEval', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT: wire Salesforce/GiftEvalPretrain into the MAMBA cell. Arrow files, non-leaking vs GIFT-Eval test; pull a representative SUBSET of .arrow OR stream (<50GB local on /workspace). Forecasting: context window -> horizon H; point (MSE/MAE) or probabilistic (CRPS/quantile) loss. FIXED held-out window set sampled once, reused every eval (normalized MASE/CRPS on the fixed windows; never iterate the full corpus). Note current mamba seq=8/d128 — a coupling to the window size (document; don't change model defs). Output: make_data_for_task mamba branch + fixed window probe. Write to /workspace/phase3/mamba_gifteval.md.` },
  { name:'p3_harness', phase:'P3', label:'P3 harness (eval/EarlyStopper)', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT the SHARED harness changes in grokking_race_v2.py for the scaled-dataset regime: (1) make_data_for_task(c,seed) dispatch on model_type returning a streaming train iterator + a fixed eval probe (preserve signature + call sites). (2) evaluate(): CAP to the fixed probe (build once at load ~1-10M tok / few-thousand windows / 50k-img subset; reuse) — the current code forwards the WHOLE (tex,tey) every call (catastrophic at scale). Hard requirement: eval cost seconds not minutes. (3) EarlyStopper: add a loss-PLATEAU criterion (no improvement over K evals) for the LM + forecasting cells; KEEP the 95% accuracy trigger for the ImageNet ViT cell (read EarlyStopper@542, early_stop_on). (4) _progressive_eval_freq@696: tune thresh/cap so total eval count stays ~250-500 over the configured 20000-step budget. Single-pass streaming for LM+timeseries (never complete an epoch). Output a unified-diff-style draft to /workspace/phase3/harness_changes.md.` },
  // ---- Phase 2: compile additions (confirmed ABSENT per COMPILE_RECONCILE.md) ----
  { name:'p2_s14_l2persist', phase:'P2', label:'P2 S1.4 L2-persistence dim', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT S1.4: expose cudaAccessPolicyWindow / L2-persistence as a TUNED dimension in compile.py. NOTE the substrate ALREADY has primitives.cuh L2PersistScope (RAII over cudaStreamSetAttribute+cudaAccessPolicyWindow, gated ENABLE_L2_PERSIST) — so the kernel side exists; the missing piece is (a) a compile.py tuned dim (hit-ratio + cudaLimitPersistingL2CacheSize set-aside size) parameterizing it, and (b) wiring it through the launch path. Read compile.py _sm90_full_space (~2122) + the _dim machinery (~1234) + primitives.cuh L2PersistScope. Keep it GENERIC/portable (config-declared, not SuperGrok-hardcoded). Draft the new _dim + macro + the wiring to /workspace/phase2/s14_l2persist.md.` },
  { name:'p2_s15_smem_carveout', phase:'P2', label:'P2 S1.5 smem carveout dim', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT S1.5: cudaFuncAttributePreferredSharedMemoryCarveout (L1-vs-shared split) + cudaFuncAttributeMaxDynamicSharedMemorySize as TUNED knobs in compile.py. NOTE kernels already set a FIXED MaxDynamicSharedMemorySize (e.g. fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:1533) but compile.py never sweeps it. Read compile.py _sm90_full_space + _dim; design the new tuned dims + the cudaFuncSetAttribute launch-wrapper plumbing. Generic/portable. Draft to /workspace/phase2/s15_smem_carveout.md.` },
  { name:'p2_s34_negcache_bugs', phase:'P2', label:'P2 S3.4 negcache + bug fixes', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT two things: (A) S3.4 cross-run NEGATIVE cache + bloom-filter dedup in compile.py — persist infeasible/compile-fail/audit-fail configs across runs (currently only within-run status="infeasible"); bloom over config hashes for O(1) dedup. (B) FIX these VERIFIED bugs (cite the lines): (1) dead `from grokking_optimizers.device_profiling import run_device_pgo_round` (compile.py:~17652 — module doesn't exist, ModuleNotFoundError → device-PGO round is a silent no-op); decide: inline the function or add the module/alias. (2) resolve_extra_hipcc_flags (~3424) doesn't skip the _MAXRREGCOUNT_UNCAPPED=-1 sentinel the NVCC sibling skips (~3355) → malformed '=-1' (gfx942 only — preserve, just fix). (3) inert ABI guard: GROK_ABI_SCHEMA exported (bindings.cpp:~115) but no Python-side __abi_schema__ assertion. Draft fixes to /workspace/phase2/s34_and_bugs.md.` },
  // ---- Phase 4: verification harness ----
  { name:'p4_verify_harness', phase:'P4', label:'P4 verify harness', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN the Phase-4 per-function silicon verification harness for the sm_90 path: for every function/method on the L3-TC path (Python + the device functions reachable via _ops), an isolation test (representative + edge inputs, real-hardware numeric check) + an ablation/wiring check (stub/remove -> confirm a measurable behavioral change in the composed system; no effect => dead/unwired => flag). Leverage the EXISTING gates (tests/hw/test_l3tc_tail_gate.py run_cell_gate, verify_all, the fp64+A/A/A oracle) rather than reinventing. Enumerate the sm_90 function surface (from the dispatch/launcher/opt_components reachability) and propose the isolation+ablation matrix + how to drive it 8-GPU-wide. Preserve gfx942/tpu. Draft to /workspace/phase4/verify_harness.md.` },
  // ---- Phase 5: dead code ----
  { name:'p5_deadcode', phase:'P5', label:'P5 dead-code removal', prompt:`${COMMON}
DESIGN+DRAFT the Phase-5 provably-dead-code removals (ONLY provably-dead; NEVER the gfx942/tpu_v6e trees; NOT the Phase1-3-owned kernel/compile/dataset files). Verified-dead candidates from the read: (1) in-file MambaModel/SelectiveSSMLayer in grokking_race_v2.py (~434-489, state_dim=16, superseded by Mamba3Model, never instantiated); (2) _maybe_wrap_cuda_graph no-op shim (grokking_race_v2.py:~895); (3) the stages_values unused local in compile.py _build_cuda/cdna/rdna_space (~1843/1959/2027 — back-compat plumbing, confirm). For EACH: prove dead (grep all refs/reachability), draft the removal diff, and note the re-validation (drift guard + verify_all) needed after. Draft to /workspace/phase5/deadcode.md.` },
