  { name:'cute_atoms', label:'available CuTe atoms', prompt:`${COMMON}
INVENTORY the CuTe device-side atoms in third_party/cutlass/include/cute/ usable INSIDE a persistent kernel (no host launch): the SM90 GMMA/wgmma MMA atoms (cute/atom/mma_traits_sm90_gmma.hpp, mma_atom.hpp), the TMA copy atoms (cute/atom/copy_traits_sm90_tma.hpp, SM90_TMA_LOAD), swizzle layouts (cute/swizzle.hpp, cute/layout.hpp), and the pipeline (cutlass/pipeline/sm90_pipeline.hpp). For EACH: how it's constructed device-side, what host-side setup it needs (e.g. TMA descriptor must be created host-side via cute::make_tma_copy then passed in), and whether it works without owning the grid. Output: the exact atoms/headers + their device-vs-host split (esp. the TMA descriptor host-creation seam).` },
