READ IN FULL: csrc/backends/cuda/sm_90/mma.cuh (the existing host-launched CUTLASS Sm90 collective usage) + how setup.py/compile.py pass CUTLASS flags (-DCUTLASS_NVCC_ARCHS=90a). Extract: how the codebase ALREADY builds TMA descriptors (cuTensorMapEncode / make_tma_copy), the CuTe patterns already present, what's reusable for the device-side rewrite, and WHY it's host-launched (the exact incompatibility with the persistent kernel). This tells us what CuTe machinery is already wired + the TMA-descriptor host seam to reuse.` },
